# Sangeetha Grantha — Cursor rules

> **Canonical source of truth: [`CLAUDE.md`](CLAUDE.md).** Architecture, Makefile/Flyway
> workflows, audit-log and commit rules, ports, layer skills, slash commands, and
> specialist subagents live there. Read it first.
>
> This file is a thin pointer so Cursor (which still auto-loads `.cursorrules`) cannot
> drift from Claude Code. An older copy here told agents to **avoid Flyway** and use the
> archived Rust CLI — the opposite of [ADR-013](application_documentation/02-architecture/decisions/ADR-013-db-migration-with-flyway.md).

## Cursor-specific files

- Always-on rules: [`.cursor/rules/`](.cursor/rules/) (`project.mdc`, `git-conventions.mdc`)
- Skills: [`.cursor/skills/`](.cursor/skills/) — layer skills and commands **mirror** [`.claude/skills/`](.claude/skills/) and [`.claude/commands/`](.claude/commands/)
- Git: [`.cursor/rules/git-conventions.mdc`](.cursor/rules/git-conventions.mdc) and [commit-policy](.agents/skills/commit-policy/SKILL.md)

## Quick reminders (authoritative text in CLAUDE.md)

- **Migrations:** Flyway only — `make migrate` / `make db-reset`. Never Liquibase, never a custom runner, never `tools/sangita-cli` (archived).
- **DB access:** `DatabaseFactory.dbQuery { }`; return `@Serializable` DTOs, never Exposed entities.
- **Audit:** every mutation writes to `AUDIT_LOG`.
- **Commits:** `TRACK-ID` when a track exists; exactly one `Ref: application_documentation/...` line; do not commit until asked.
- **Versions:** [current-versions.md](application_documentation/00-meta/current-versions.md) — do not hardcode versions here.
